From ea96ecaccd446fc54b49ab1417553f725e100eff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Tada Antunes <leonardotada@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:11:56 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 56/56] gc: speed small-heap appendable alloc for format/qalloc
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Quiet-frame residual on the paced engine --worst bench was mutator
allocation (format/Appender qalloc), not markers or madvise. Preserve
APPENDABLE on small realloc, cache BlkInfo for the just-allocated block,
skip a second memset when pointer slots were zeroed on free, write fresh
slot metadata without a hasMetadata probe, and floor NO_SCAN appendable
to 64 bytes so a typical format line fits one qalloc.

Measured DMD --worst (5 runs, this machine): mean ~6.4–6.7 ms vs
druntime ~5.2–5.5 ms (~1.23–1.27×; was ~1.55×). worst-safe mean ties;
correctness battery passes. openworld still ~1.3×.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
